Question 04 — Bank Account System

A Bank Account System manages different types of bank accounts. Each account has an account number and balance, but there are specialized accounts such as SavingsAccount and CurrentAccount.

Each Account contains an ATMCard that stores card details, meaning ATMCard is a part of Account and cannot exist without it.

Additionally, the bank has multiple Customers, and each Customer is associated with an Account. However, a Customer can exist independently of a specific account.

Different types of accounts have unique implementations of the showAccountType() method, which need to be overridden.

a) Implement a class called Account with accountNumber(String) and balance(double) attributes.
i. Create a method called showAccountType() that prints a generic account message.

b) Create two classes called SavingsAccount and CurrentAccount as subclasses of Account.
i. Override the showAccountType() method.

c) Implement an ATMCard class with cardNumber(String) as an attribute.
i. The ATMCard should be part of Account using Composition and initialized within the Account constructor.

d) Create a class called Customer with customerName(String) and contactNumber(String) attributes.
i. A Customer should be associated with Account using Aggregation.

e) Modify SavingsAccount and CurrentAccount to include a Customer for each class.

f) Create a BankApp class with a main method to:
i. Create SavingsAccount and CurrentAccount objects with ATMCard.
ii. Assign Customers to those accounts.
iii. Call showAccountType() and display full details.

